    "sha": "22d559805c9ebd3333424bd5aba93dc69ffd7627",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVmlK7doAKDIyZDU1OTgwNWM5ZWJkMzMzMzQyNGJkNWFiYTkzZGM2OWZmZDc2Mjc",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-08T23:27:02Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-08T23:27:02Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(post): Fanuc probe result folds the expected value's sign into the operator\n\nAn edge or outside-corner probe whose expected value is negative in the\nwork offset wrote a doubled sign: `#190=#100--17` for the deviation and\n`IF[ABS[#5061--12]LT0.001]` for the no-contact check. Both now go through\none helper, minusU, which folds the sign into the operator (`#100+17`) and\nwrites no term for a value that formats to zero (`#190=#100`). Output stays\nin the unbracketed macro B form `#i=#j+#k`; the bore-centre golden is\nunchanged.\n\nPinned by edge_probe_at_negative_x_folds_the_sign,\ncorner_probe_at_negative_xy_folds_both_signs and\nedge_probe_at_zero_writes_the_bare_mean (fanuc_post), with new goldens\nnc/fanuc/probe_edge_negative_x.nc and probe_corner_negative.nc; every\nposted line is checked for `--`, `+-` and `-+`.\n\nFixes #377\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
